{"title":"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Hints\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Hints</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Dan Schwarz, Romania</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> with integer coefficients, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be a positive integer.  Consider the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4c1afb30c3a14422986040fa5faf1e5e74c482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x) = P( P ( \\ldots P(P(x)) \\ldots ))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> occurs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> times.  Prove that there are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d777f4f49e93e545adc4f6c84bb9d0b69cc9394b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(t)=t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use the notation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae2062cebaa431374a76eb15bb4d931cc44c05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P^k(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1.</b> The problem statement holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da29376ccb80f19219cb4c67a5f9232a231d97d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, \\dotsc, a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbdab1fb0b95904f8412dad77ca4a7c9dbd902c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, \\dotsc, b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> are integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a2e6f4bf8b0fca25840cd25f386e0bd807f10ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a_j) = b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb6d5ef65f74d75a61ae9cc36b2240d5e71b37b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(b_j) = a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> for all indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />.  Let the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edbe4188da702b90855fddb9aef610af9ef80dde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ a_1, \\dotsc, a_k, b_1, \\dotsc, b_k \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> distinct elements.  It suffices to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab952f09cb2f3c8ce4c10b1d554032768612dd9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\deg (P) \\ge m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db93d14dd35737b697c64f2125430e90081c7efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j = b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> for all indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, then the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e1968035113e4d6eae31a100968e429bc7d88209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> has at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> roots; since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is not linear, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad7e3600346aa7119f459cea371a368a779b05c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\deg P \\ge m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> by the division algorithm.\n</p><p>Suppose on the other hand that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/981b510a60a7cd6f39a47d02463a99e20f07e8f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\neq b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, for some index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />.  In this case, we claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e91536f752468414403acd583159c32e2d90f901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j + b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> is constant for every index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />.  Indeed, we note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/7826bdf97edf5b5197281ce7f2a646ef3577ea8e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_j - a_i \\mid P(a_j) - P(a_i) = b_j - b_i \\mid P(b_j) - P(b_i) = a_j - a_i ,\\]\" width=\"458\" height=\"19\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c193e36de5f5425d50c6756c65b98a7838a69c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert a_j - a_i \\rvert = \\lvert b_j - b_i \\rvert$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />.  Similarly,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/2220e213cf558eb2f054b3edec5b174154f5d173.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_j - b_i \\mid P(a_j) - P(b_i) = b_j - a_i \\mid P(b_j) - P(a_i) = a_j - b_i,\\]\" width=\"456\" height=\"19\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/46055225503daf26f897a9b0a6fc97b77a6af32b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert a_j - b_i \\rvert = \\lvert b_j - a_i \\rvert$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd3dc1fd38e93b67c5b8eb18e696ffa4ce64f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j + b_j = a_i + b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>This proves our claim.  It follows that the polynomial\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221c1c0d5cdf66515d173caffe1d50b1ad7febcb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(x) - \\left( a_i + b_i - x \\right)\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\nhas at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> roots.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is not linear it follows again that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad7e3600346aa7119f459cea371a368a779b05c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\deg P \\ge m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />, as desired.  Thus the lemma is proven.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2.</b> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/2/6c2e406c40e39acf94f6be33466942ace9b39003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P^r(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac96ef908605d540d4e5b8e22a97be1e6c8dc5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P^2(a) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  Let us denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d12f65f644c817caa7e9e3e7e81d43716fbdc9c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde092e54ed3bbb03506d5235d23e2e29fea15b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j = P^j(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" />, for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a76ca40ccd4804eb798c6bec3acd4bb09d49798a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 = a_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fc5fb30ccf7d297f91a55c33f7cea4560be7c77.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_1 - a_0 &amp;\\mid P(a_1)- P(a_0) = a_2-a_1 \\\\ &amp;\\mid P(a_2) - P(a_1) = a_3 - a_2 \\\\ &amp;\\vdots \\\\ &amp;\\mid P(a_r)- P(a_{r-1}) = a_1 - a_0 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"285\" height=\"108\" />\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/6226b8b7fa6516986db1430bd0aedda50dc828dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert a_{j+1} - a_j \\rvert$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> is constant for all indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />; let us abbreviate this quantity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Now, since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64e6663a0ecbab752746c03406f6d405f8842caf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1-a_0) + (a_2-a_1) + \\dotsb + (a_r-a_{r-1}) = a_r-a_0 = 0,\\]\" width=\"432\" height=\"18\" />\nit follows that for some index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc51122b3abc5f511ace2d56c08f343a44ec489.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_j - a_{j+1} = -(a_{j+1} - a_{j+2}),\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"19\" />\nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d9b2f0fe3e4b5aafd6295a6982b039b0b6494d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j = a_{j+2} = P^2(a_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7323b670e7cb273cc3b00c82b2c75c9c792d3932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = a_r = P^{r-j}(a_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"19\" />, it then follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac96ef908605d540d4e5b8e22a97be1e6c8dc5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P^2(a) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"19\" />, as desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Now, if there are more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/92576f11762e6b550104a37bfd16ff37855c2618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(t) = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, then by Lemma 2, there are more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac322c7133a0eb87b269f4b19feed52368401ea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P^2(t) = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />, which is a contradiction by Lemma 1.  Thus the problem is solved.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Hints\">Hints</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Hints\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Try to use contradiction:\nOn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5ddf80b3bc0174970bfcf615fcfde94e15b863e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x_1)=x_1,...,Q(x_{n+1})=x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" />. \n(WLOG suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae2a070a136341f9f23a7211cf019d7f463581f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1&lt;...&lt;x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />.)\n</p><p>Think of using the theorem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d27cb96347f828b25a546969973d65a5b53812f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b \\mid f(a)-f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Try to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78786b8b877a47146c5407babe5e05f22d68f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1),...,P(x_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> is either increasing or decreasing.\n</p><p>Construct a polynomial to give the final contradiction by keeping in mind the theorem:\nIf the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249fee52f4450606c3c1bdc7c4fabb697a35156f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) - a= 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a constant) has more roots than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7c84b27cf83aac8065733e103cca38e53519ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$deg(f)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/8883d3e33dee1add34d76f65000a8031721557b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)- a = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73e2add991c49a74839a1ad65504df2836cc06ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note:\nWe will denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129301bf78e77acce380a2df8cee8790d8b19d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(...(P(x))....)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> occurs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> times) as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/07286a66bad883a08aaaef64004ae0e555d3df30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> throughout the proof, for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08ff8ea020546fb6e8c90abbfb0b50802eee802d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>For the sake of contradiction, let the problem statement be false.\nFor convinience's sake, let the stated equation thus have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> solutions:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/10658c04d3b0cd76ed10ab7a1ec133a20eb2e44e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k(x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />,...,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f106eaeecd863b286e7ae2ffdf907ab7c9cea14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k(x_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Without loss of generality, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f03892f824e63d1d076e9842240444821ec1a12a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 &lt; ... &lt;x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is defined over the integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffdfd164f6797b3479812d9fb44120c1b9e88427.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i - x_j \\mid P(x_i) - P(x_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" /> for all distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d9dbe8588e6243350fc642973b9365304100da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" />.\nAlso, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f069485cf1df3d372ff004b487c471d96fd54f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_i) - P(x_j) \\mid P_2(x_i) - P_2(x_j) \\mid ... \\mid P_k(x_i) - P_k(x_j) = x_i - x_j.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"505\" height=\"20\" />\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a805dba593f96f3d2aed357155ce36b7e09e685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P(x_i) - P(x_j)| = x_i - x_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"204\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d3e320fd45639d428d4e09c3e8e78c93b13af6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&gt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nClaim.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da9274f0e993149a2914af409ff42d44c66810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_i) \\neq P(x_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743293b410b7d3bdf6a048265134ab7aa60b38b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\neq j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Proof.\n</p><p>For the sake of contradiction, suppose the claim statement is wrong.\n</p><p>Then, for some distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887919dfbc86eebc29e0373f98f97dbf23a0ae23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i,j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a466e5b7a1c7d1d5e9def1f8bda524f35a4e09d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_i)=P(x_j) =&gt;|P(x_i)-P(x_j)|=0=&gt; x_i=x_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"406\" height=\"20\" />, a contradiction.\n</p><p>Hence, our claim is proved.\n</p><p><br />\nClaim.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78786b8b877a47146c5407babe5e05f22d68f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1),...,P(x_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> is either increasing or decreasing.\n</p><p>Proof.\n</p><p>We will only prove the decreasing part, as the increasing part is similar.\n</p><p>For the sake of contradiction, suppose the claim statement is wrong.\nThen, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f0dac309c1f2f12817f564c82b084b6e0d725b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_{i-1})&gt;P(x_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca6175a953378103ae8d14e0094c4558e85fde3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_i)&lt;P(x_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b934ca27da25038445a99a7898871ee70d0d9ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> (that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/180531a0ec58edadccb218297155ae1ba3a02c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1)&gt;...&gt;P(x_{i-1})&gt;P(x_i)&lt;P(x_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"327\" height=\"20\" />).\n</p><p>For convinience's sake, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3e5193f4abdbaf8c424028753f296dac345eb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=2$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b5fc6016411a953c8eae382a984edb4f5ca10c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P(x_1)-P(x_2)|=P(x_1)-P(x_2)=x_2-x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"347\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf8c1a8cec80a3d513f354395aebafae6fee89f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P(x_3)-P(x_2)|=P(x_3)-P(x_2)=x_3-x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"347\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Adding, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b975b0aedbbe6fc9db9d3006797b0ba04cc64b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P(x_1)+P(x_3))-2 \\cdot P(x_2) = x_3 - x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"303\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5cd09dd7afdc3cff06d843e25f0f58544a21d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 - x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> will either be substituted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c739cdc6fb2b73dc8ddc7500f93ddf31a7ebcd06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1)-P(x_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a715859449e9e6655f5cd9acce7c7a22202a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_3)-P(x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Either way, we get a contradiction to our previous claim.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635067e18c471524a57699601248a93faf00fb34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_2)&gt;P(x_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. \nSimilarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a0420f3613872bbe6faf7678043496e86b5adfb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_3)&gt;P(x_4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />,...,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2989121203acbfd073b2981abfc546b298b5c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_n)&gt;P(x_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c748da2bce15e183a11b8a9c65ed73c4d921f67a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1)&gt;...&gt;P(x_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>One may similarly prove the increasing part.\n</p><p>Hence, our claim is proved.\n</p><p><br />\nCase 1, The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78786b8b877a47146c5407babe5e05f22d68f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1),...,P(x_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> is increasing:\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/28552985373f357bea924e918ff0f738ef683fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(x)=(P(x)-x)-(P(x_1)-x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"272\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c38da9daed5d383f5d93251d18f4f182f79d571a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> roots: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d253292068909be5421b191d637790a8075ec38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,...,x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> from our previous claim, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f34fac49d0b89bb42afefb250a36b0c77c8c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$deg(T)=deg(P)=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />, a contradiction.\n</p><p>One may similarly show the contradiction if the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78786b8b877a47146c5407babe5e05f22d68f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x_1),...,P(x_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> is decreasing, by just replacing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c38da9daed5d383f5d93251d18f4f182f79d571a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nHence, we get our desired contradiction, and thus we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 1</a>, which implies a special case of this problem</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO\" title=\"2006 IMO\">2006 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211731\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.092 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 678/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0